  "excerpt": "Beef chuck slow-braised in the oven with red wine vinegar, stock, and aromatics until it is fork-tender and deeply savoury. This follows the American short rib braise method: a good sear, a long low cook, and a sauce that reduces to a glossy coating. Worth every minute.",
